Rule 1 (all-elements min requires non-empty input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 2 (all-elements min does not support complex dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 3 (all-elements min with out: out must be a scalar tensor of same dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 0 ∧ dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (pairwise min: inputs and out must have identical shapes and dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i) ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (pairwise min does not support complex dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 10)
>>
Rule 6 (reduction dim must be within valid range)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= (0 - ndim(v_1)) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 7 (reduction dim must have non-zero size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 ≥ 0 then shape(v_1, v_2) > 0 else shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) + v_2) > 0
>>
Rule 11 (all-elements min without dim: empty tensors require specifying dim; enforce non-emptiness here)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0)
